      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interrupted is classified as finished.\n\n`COMPLETED_TASK_STATES` includes `Interrupted`. In bmcweb that state is still active: it emits `TaskEvent.TaskPaused`, and `getTaskToRemove()` keeps `Interrupted` in the active set alongside Running, Pending, Starting, and Suspended. Polling stops, so a task that resumes to Running stays stale until the window is focused.\n\nConsider mapping `Interrupted`, `Stopping`, and `Cancelling` as active. In those cases, the service should never complete; poll it for as long as the page is open (worth a cap or a slower interval)",
