      "side": 1,
      "message": "The table omits the fields that explain the task.\n\nbmcweb sets Name to \"Task {id}\". The first column is labeled “Task Description”, so on OpenBMC it shows Task 3. `TaskState` and `TaskStatus` are not columns. Messages are stored on TaskDisplay and never rendered. The strings `pageTasks.table.state` and `pageTasks.details.*` are unused.\n\nFor a running dump, `PercentComplete` stays 0 until the end (percentComplete defaults to 0 in bmcweb). The action cell is blank unless TaskMonitor is set, in which case it is only Cancel. A finished Exception task is a red status-icon whose tooltip is the enum name Exception. StatusIcon has no title prop; the attribute falls through to the \u003cspan\u003e.\n\nWe need to keep the Redfish resource and show those messages. A firmware task started elsewhere should be picked up from the collection (and from SSE TaskStarted events) and shown in a global banner without sending the user to a logs page. This page can still be the inventory. It needs a state column, and the first Messages[].Message (and Resolution on failure) in the row or an expand. TaskStatus of Warning or Critical should not share the success icon used for Completed.",
